    },
    {
      "content": "speaking_too_quickly",
      "name": "Alexander Tran",
      "time": "2026-09-02T20:51:39.643705",
      "type": "moment",
      "user_id": "6592087457742848"
    },
    {
      "content": "Team, but if you already have stuff going on like you're disassembling the, the dining room table or any or anything else like that which is already extra that stuff that we factor out whenever we're flushing out our estimates. We usually intend to be the ones to handle the disassemble. You should never fill obligated to do that. Unless you're just looking for ways to save time. But if all you do is just reconcile all of your boxes, I feel pretty confident that you'll be able to hopefully shoot underneath that four and a half. But with four and a half hour load up and let's say about a four hour drive that first day. We're looking at about eight and a half hours maybe potentially a little bit more if we do stop by the house to unload the primary bedroom Furner furniture for you, but if we do that you may, although you may have a little bit of a higher first day than the eight and a half hours maybe a little bit closer to nine or something like that, it's just gonna translate in less time for the following unload day at the at the storage unit but all things considered. I still feel like you're floating right around that four K, estimate. It's at $4,105 to, to be specific the only thing that would influence that outside of the expenses associated with this being out of town and the hourly rate is just, if you decided you wanted to leave a pad deposit meaning you wanted to leave some of the items wrapped up and moving blankets.",
